  "user_scenario": "Rosalind Ashby is seventy-five and telephones from 2135550394 mid-afternoon, with a letter from an ambulatory surgery centre in front of her and her reading glasses pushed up into her hair. Back in February she had a shoulder repair at a place her surgeon sent her to, and the plan turned it down; the practice has now sent her the whole amount and she says she is quite certain the approval came through before she ever went in, because the surgeon's office told her so on the telephone at the time. What she wants is for somebody to look again at the surgery they turned down and put right what she actually owes on it. She is quick and a little dry about it, not angry, but she wants an answer today rather than another letter.\n\nShe is content for the representative to go through whatever they need to on her record, and says so early; if there is anything only she can do, she will do it herself there and then while she is on the line, so long as somebody tells her in plain words what it is.\n\nAsked how to find her, she gives her name and then the number from her Medicare card, 1AE8HK3PQ47, reading the letters out slowly, and if anything further is wanted she gives the ZIP code at home, 93562. She will give her date of birth if asked, the eighth of June 1951, and she mentions that she lives alone and has never given anybody authority to speak for her.\n\nAsked about the surgery itself, she says it was her right shoulder, that it was done in February at the centre on the letter, and that she never saw a bill for it until now. Asked what she has paid the plan, she says she has paid what came, sometimes late, and cannot put a figure on it; she asks the representative to read the account rather than take her word for it. Asked whether she holds any of the extra benefits, she says she has a dental rider, and that she thinks she may have fallen a month or two behind on what it costs.\n\nIf the representative tells her that something on her record has to be settled before they can deal with the surgery, she says that is fine and to do whatever the rules require, and she does not ask what it is. If the representative unlocks something and hands it to her to do in her own name, she says she is ready, listens to the figure, and does it. Once she is told what she owes on the surgery after the correction, she reads the amount back once, says that sounds more like it, and rings off without asking for anything else.",
